Subject: [PATCH 209/209] docs(area): AreaComponents README

User-facing documentation for the Area Components feature, modelled on the
CinematicCamera README: what it is, how to install it, and how to use it.

- install/deploy: AreaComponents.dll to both the engine and the project bin,
  AreaComponentsEditor.dll to EditorPlugins, the rebuilt Sandbox binaries
  (the editor core gained the generic component-edit hook), and the
  .cryproject plugin entry.
- concept: one shape component per entity (Box, Sphere, Polygon, Spline,
  mutually exclusive) plus function components on the same entity (Area,
  Trigger Bounds, Gravity Volume, Distributor); legacy Area objects coexist
  untouched; vis areas/portals/occluders out of scope.
- creating: the four Create -> Area presets and their gestures, and the
  Add Component route for bare shapes and functions.
- editing: Edit Shape, drag/insert/delete/snap, outline picking, F framing,
  one undo step per gesture, Recenter Pivot.
- property reference for all eight components with the inspector labels and
  defaults, including the sphere's largest-axis scale rule, Height 0 =
  infinite, the spline's smoothing/tension/frame modes and the distributor's
  spacing, alignment, stretch and bake options.
- behaviour notes: entity-owned instances are not exported, links resolve for
  later layers and spawns, the hidden proxy leaves no <Area> node, the closed
  parallel-transport seam.
- known limits from the stage reports, and the console entries
  (area_SplineSelfTest, es_DrawAreas).

